loss":"one"}],"gloss":"one"},{"surface":"பகல்","parts":[{"text":"பகல்","lemma":"pakal","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"day"},{"surface":"வாழ்க்கைக்கு","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்க்கை","lemma":"vāḻkkai","gloss":"life"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"for"}],"gloss":"for a life"},{"surface":"உலமருவோரே","parts":[{"text":"உலமர்","lemma":"ulamar","gloss":"wander in distress"},{"text":"உவோர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"those who"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"those who wander in distress indeed"}]}],"literal":"If water overflows, there is no dam; if fire rages, / there is no shade to shelter living beings; / if wind blows hard, there is no strength to resist; with abounding glory, / like those elements is Valuthi of furious war. / Saying 'Cool Tamil land is not common property', not tolerating it, confronting in war, / 'If he desires tribute, let him take it,' saying, / the kings who gave have ceased to tremble. / Pitiable indeed, very pitiable are those who lost his grace! / Like the winged termites of the red anthill / built with great difficulty by many tiny termites, / they wander in distress for a single day's life.","translation":"When water overflows, no dam can hold it. When fire rages, there is no shade to shelter living beings. When the wind blows hard, no strength can resist it. Abounding in glory, Valuthi of furious war is like those elements. Refusing to tolerate anyone saying 'Cool Tamil land is common property', he confronts them in war. The kings who yielded, saying, 'If he desires tribute, let him take it,' have ceased to tremble. But oh, how pitiable are those who lost his grace! Like the winged termites that emerge from a red anthill built with immense effort by many tiny termites, only to perish, they wander in distress for a single day's life.","modern":"வெள்ளம் பெருகினால் அதைத் தடுக்கும் அணை இல்லை. நெருப்பு மிகுந்தால் மன்னுயிர்களைக் காக்கும் நிழல் இல்லை. காற்று மிகையாக வீசினால் அதை எதிர்க்கும் வலிமை இல்லை. அவற்றைப் போன்ற ஆற்றலும் மிகுந்த புகழும் உடையவன் சினந்து போர் செய்யும் மாறன் வழுதி. 'குளிர்ந்த தமிழ் நாடு அனைவருக்கும் பொதுவானது' என்று பிறர் கூறுவதைப் பொறுக்காமல், அவன் போரிட எழுந்தான். 'அவன் திறை கேட்கிறான் என்றால், அதை அவனிடமே கொடுத்துவிடுங்கள்' என்று பணிந்து கொடுத்த மன்னர்கள் நடுக்கம் நீங்கி வாழ்கிறார்கள். ஆனால், அவனது அருளைப் பெறாமல் இழந்தவர்கள் மிகவும் இரங்கத்தக்கவர்கள்! பல சிறிய கறையான்கள் மிகவும் பாடுபட்டு எழுப்பிய செம்மண் புற்றிலிருந்து வெளிப்படும் ஈசல்கள் போல, ஒரே ஒரு நாள் வாழ்க்கைக்காக அவர்கள் அலைந்து வருந்துகிறார்கள்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Aiyūr Muṭavaṉār praises the Pandya king Māṟaṉ Vaḻuti, who died at Kūṭakāram. The poet compares the king's unstoppable power in battle to the destructive forces of nature, such as overflowing water, raging fire, and violent wind. The king is fiercely protective of his land and cannot tolerate anyone claiming that the cool Tamil land is common property. Those kings who submitted to him and paid tribute are safe and have ceased to tremble. However, those who resisted and lost his grace are highly pitiable. They are compared to winged termites that emerge from a red anthill built with immense effort by tiny termites, only to perish after a single day of wandering in distress.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.3],[1.3,2.0],[2.0,2.65],[2.65,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.3],[4.3,4.5],[4.5,5.7],[5.7,5.9],[5.9,6.7],[6.7,7.26],[7.26,7.6],[7.6,7.8],[7.8,8.2],[8.2,8.76],[8.76,9.6],[9.6,9.9],[9.9,10.3],[10.3,10.5],[10.5,10.8],[10.8,11.0],[11.0,11.49],[11.49,12.3],[12.3,12.7],[12.7,12.96],[12.96,13.22],[13.22,13.57],[13.57,13.92],[13.92,14.36],[14.36,14.5],[14.5,15.19],[15.19,15.88],[15.88,16.4],[16.4,17.15],[17.15,17.9],[18.64,19.14],[19.14,19.44],[19.44,20.14],[20.14,20.74],[20.74,21.18],[21.18,21.44],[21.44,21.84],[21.84,22.39],[22.39,23.04],[23.36,24.09],[24.09,24.34]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.59],[1.59,2.1],[2.1,2.75],[2.75,3.4],[3.4,3.7],[3.7,4.4],[4.4,4.66],[4.66,6.2],[6.2,6.4],[6.4,7.1],[7.1,8.1],[8.1,8.3],[8.3,8.5],[8.5,9.0],[9.0,9.64],[9.64,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.3],[11.3,11.6],[11.6,11.9],[11.9,12.2],[12.2,12.76],[12.76,13.7],[13.7,14.1],[14.1,14.6],[14.7,15.0],[15.0,15.8],[15.8,16.03],[16.03,16.77],[16.77,17.21],[17.21,17.81],[17.81,18.4],[18.4,18.9],[18.9,19.8],[19.8,20.1],[20.92,21.52],[21.52,21.82],[21.82,22.52],[22.52,23.22],[23.22,23.84],[23.84,24.22],[24.22,24.62],[24.62,25.26],[25.26,26.02],[26.02,27.12],[27.25,27.39]]},"sync":[[["நீர்","water"],["மிகின்","if (it) exceeds"]],[["சிறையும்","even a dam"]],[["இல்லை","there is none"]],[["தீ","fire"],["மிகின்","if (it) rages"]],[["மன்னுயிர்","abiding lives"]],[["நிழற்றும்","which gives shade"]],[["நிழலும்","even a shade"]],[["இல்லை","there is none"]],[["வளி","wind"],["மிகின்","if (it) blows hard"]],[["வலியும்","even strength"]],[["இல்லை","there is none"]],[["ஒளி","glory"],["மிக்கு","having abounded"]],[["அவற்றோர்","with those elements"]],[["அன்ன","like"]],[["சினப்போர்","angry battle"]],[["வழுதி","Valuthi (Pandya king)"]],[["தண்","cool"]],[["தமிழ்","Tamil land"]],[["பொது","common"]],[["என","as saying"]],[["பொறாஅன்","not tolerating"]],[["போர்","war"]],[["எதிர்ந்து","having confronted"]],[["கொண்டி","tribute"]],[["வேண்டுவன்","he who desires"]],[["ஆயின்","if so"]],[["கொள்க","let him take"]],[["என","saying"]],[["கொடுத்த","who gave"]],[["மன்னர்","kings"]],[["நடுக்கற்றனரே","they ceased to tremble indeed"]],[["நடுக்கற்றனரே","they ceased to tremble indeed"]],[["அளியரோ","pitiable indeed!"]],[["அளியர்","pitiable ones"]],[["அவன்","his"]],[["அளி","grace"],["இழந்தோரே","those who lost indeed"]],[["இழந்தோரே","those who lost indeed"]],[["நுண்","tiny"],["பல்","many"]],[["சிதலை","termites"]],[["அரிது","with difficulty"],["முயன்று","having strived"]],[["எடுத்த","which was built"]],[["செம்புற்று","red anthill"]],[["ஈயல்","winged termites"]],[["போல","like"]],[["ஒரு","one"],["பகல்","day"]],[["வாழ்க்கைக்கு","for a life"]],[["உலமருவோரே","those who wander in distress indeed"]],[["உலமருவோரே","those who wander in distress indeed"]]]}